{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כי יהיה ריב", :translit "ki yihyeh riv", :gloss "when there is a dispute"} {:he "ריב", :translit "riv", :gloss "dispute"} {:he "לקט", :translit "leket", :gloss "glean"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah parshiyot: juxtaposition of the topic of dispute (Deut 25:1) with the topic of gleanings (Deut 24:19–22)"}], :frame {:text "Deut 24:19–22 commands the farmer to leave gleanings (leket), forgotten sheaves (shikheḥah), and the corner (pe'ah) for the poor, the stranger, the widow, and the orphan. Ba'al HaTurim reads the juxtaposition of that passage with the opening of Deut 25:1 ('When there is a dispute') as signaling that the poor themselves come to blows over these leftover gifts.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 24:19–22" "Deuteronomy 25:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "המשפט ושפטום", :translit "hamishpat veshafetum", :gloss "the judgment and you shall judge them"} {:he "השופט", :translit "hashofet", :gloss "the judge"} {:he "שמכות בשלשה", :translit "she-makot bishloshah", :gloss "that lashes with three"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :notarikon, :word "השופט", :expansion ["שמכות" "בשלשה"]}], :frame {:text "Makkot 3b establishes that lashes are administered by a court of three judges. Ba'al HaTurim reads the letters of השופט (which appear in the phrase המשפט ושפטום) as a compressed signal of this rule: ש-מכות ב-שלשה, 'lashes [are administered] by three.'", :sources ["Makkot 3b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Semikhah parshiyot: juxtaposition of the topic of dispute (Deut 25:1) with the topic of gleanings (Deut 24:19–22)", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :notarikon, :word "השופט", :expansion ["שמכות" "בשלשה"], :initials ["ש" "ב"], :by :selah, :initials-match? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-13T00:34:06.472514789Z", :model "glm-5.2"}